 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Independence of the scheme structure",
 "statement": "Let $a\\colon Z\\to X$ and $b\\colon Z'\\to X$ be immersions with the same\nimage. Then $a^*\\mathcal F$ is finite locally constant if and only if\n$b^*\\mathcal F$ is.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-proper-base-change/sk-thm-p1/lemma-constructible-immersion-independence.md",
  "place": "node lemma-constructible-immersion-independence, order 1169"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-constructible-finite-locally-constant"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Let $W=Z\\times_XZ'$ with projections $p\\colon W\\to Z$ and $q\\colon W\\to Z'$.\nThe projection $p$ is an immersion, as a base change of $b$, and it is\nsurjective, its image being $a^{-1}(b(Z'))=a^{-1}(a(Z))=Z$. A surjective\nimmersion is a surjective closed immersion (an immersion is a closed\nimmersion into an open subscheme, and surjectivity forces that open to be\neverything), hence a universal homeomorphism. The same holds for $q$. Now\n$p^*a^*\\mathcal F\\cong q^*b^*\\mathcal F$, both being the pullback along\n$a\\circ p=b\\circ q$, so by\n[lemma-constructible-universal-homeomorphism-invariance] applied to\n$p$ and to $q$, $a^*\\mathcal F$ is finite locally constant if and only if\n$p^*a^*\\mathcal F$ is, if and only if $q^*b^*\\mathcal F$ is, if and only if\n$b^*\\mathcal F$ is.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-constructible-universal-homeomorphism-invariance"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
